</person-group><article-title>Apolipoprotein A1-Encoding Recombinant Adenovirus Remodels Cholesterol Metabolism in Tumors and the Tumor Microenvironment to Inhibit Hepatocellular Carcinoma</article-title><source>Transl. Res. J. Lab. Clin. Med.</source><year>2025</year><volume>275</volume><fpage>18</fpage><lpage>31</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.trsl.2024.10.003</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">39528003</pub-id></element-citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-group><fig position="float" id="animals-15-03603-f001" orientation="portrait"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>Nontoxic induction of steatosis by oleic acid in duck hepatocytes. (<bold>A</bold>) Cell viability (CCK-8 assay) after OA treatment. (<bold>B</bold>) Intracellular triglyceride (TG) levels. The data are reported as the mean ± SD on the basis of n = 3 independent biological replicates (cells from distinct embryos). <sup>a,b,c,d</sup> Significant differences are shown in superscript letters, with different letters representing significant differences (<italic toggle="yes">p</italic> &lt; 0.05). (<bold>C</bold>) Linear correlation between OA concentration and TG content. R<sup>2</sup> and <italic toggle="yes">p</italic>-values are shown.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" position="float" orientation="portrait" xlink:href="animals-15-03603-g001.jpg"><?image-name animals-15-03603-g001.jpg?><?image-size 122182?><?image-md5 d85425783fdf4a1031775a077aac7a92?><?image-image-server-status LOAD_COMPLETED?><?image-original-height 3221?><?image-original-width 3298?><?image-scaled-height 715?><?image-scaled-width 732?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/a1db/12729497/d85425783fdf/animals-15-03603-g001.jpg?><?thumb-name animals-15-03603-g001.gif?><?thumb-size 7582?><?thumb-md5 8b1ff3a855b4c7bda6ff0cd38c469e58?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 98?><?thumb-scaled-width 100?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/a1db/12729497/8b1ff3a855b4/animals-15-03603-g001.gif?></graphic></fig><fig position="float" id="animals-15-03603-f002" orientation="portrait"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>OA concentration-dependent lipid accumulation in duck hepatocytes. (<bold>A</bold>) Oil Red O staining of lipid droplets after OA treatment. Objective lens magnification: 20×. (<bold>B</bold>) Quantification of lipid accumulation from (<bold>A</bold>). The data are reported as the mean ± SD on the basis of n = 3 independent biological replicates (cells from distinct embryos). <sup>a,b,c</sup> Significant differences are shown in superscript letters, with different letters representing significant differences (<italic toggle="yes">p</italic> &lt; 0.05). (<bold>C</bold>) Linear correlation between OA concentration and lipid content at indicated times. R<sup>2</sup> and <italic toggle="yes">p</italic>-values are shown.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" position="float" orientation="portrait" xlink:href="animals-15-03603-g002.jpg"><?image-name animals-15-03603-g002.jpg?><?image-size 182627?><?image-md5 62e7a9cc06caa4cd1bbe3b5c2cf92ed1?><?image-image-server-status LOAD_COMPLETED?><?image-original-height 2993?><?image-original-width 3091?><?image-scaled-height 748?><?image-scaled-width 772?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/a1db/12729497/62e7a9cc06ca/animals-15-03603-g002.jpg?><?thumb-name animals-15-03603-g002.gif?><?thumb-size 9068?><?thumb-md5 e1617b61b1213adc4b3eaf25a72ad419?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 97?><?thumb-scaled-width 100?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/a1db/12729497/e1617b61b121/animals-15-03603-g002.gif?></graphic></fig><fig position="float" id="animals-15-03603-f003" orientation="portrait"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>Transcriptomic profiling of OA-treated duck hepatocytes. (<bold>A</bold>) The number of genes detected per sample after quality control and filtering. (<bold>B</bold>) PCA showing separation between control and OA-treated groups. (<bold>C</bold>) Volcano plot of DEGs (adjusted <italic toggle="yes">p</italic> &lt; 0.05, |log<sub>2</sub>FC| &gt; 1.5). (<bold>D</bold>) Radar chart of top 30 DEGs by fold change. A: 150 μM OA cells for 48 h; B: 0 μM OA cells for 48 h.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" position="float" orientation="portrait" xlink:href="animals-15-03603-g003.jpg"><?image-name animals-15-03603-g003.jpg?><?image-size 128510?><?image-md5 b63726a54da00f3d20c95d8f29cd21cf?><?image-image-server-status LOAD_COMPLETED?><?image-original-height 3354?><?image-original-width 3301?><?image-scaled-height 745?><?image-scaled-width 733?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/a1db/12729497/b63726a54da0/animals-15-03603-g003.jpg?><?thumb-name animals-15-03603-g003.gif?><?thumb-size 7822?><?thumb-md5 567a631083591d0189282cdb3a965335?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 102?><?thumb-scaled-width 100?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/a1db/12729497/567a63108359/animals-15-03603-g003.gif?></graphic></fig><fig position="float" id="animals-15-03603-f004" orientation="portrait"><label>Figure 4</label><caption><p>GO and KEGG enrichment analysis of DEGs. (<bold>A</bold>) The GO enrichment of DEGs. (<bold>B</bold>) The KEGG pathway analysis of DEGs.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" position="float" orientation="portrait" xlink:href="animals-15-03603-g004.jpg"><?image-name animals-15-03603-g004.jpg?><?image-size 201667?><?image-md5 c72c1a7fdc337f5066c0c06c011cd740?><?image-image-server-status LOAD_COMPLETED?><?image-original-height 4558?><?image-original-width 3330?><?image-scaled-height 1013?><?image-scaled-width 740?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/a1db/12729497/c72c1a7fdc33/animals-15-03603-g004.jpg?><?thumb-name animals-15-03603-g004.gif?><?thumb-size 8957?><?thumb-md5 949638f1e72ef99a1cbe2de376aec1bc?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 137?><?thumb-scaled-width 100?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/a1db/12729497/949638f1e72e/animals-15-03603-g004.gif?></graphic></fig><fig position="float" id="animals-15-03603-f005" orientation="portrait"><label>Figure 5</label><caption><p>Concordance between qPCR and RNA-seq results for 17 DEGs. The data are reported as the mean ± SD on the basis of n = 3 independent biological replicates (cells from distinct embryos).</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" position="float" orientation="portrait" xlink:href="animals-15-03603-g005.jpg"><?image-name animals-15-03603-g005.jpg?><?image-size 67656?><?image-md5 015a605aaf9305c88746aace20e2676d?><?image-image-server-status LOAD_COMPLETED?><?image-original-height 1980?><?image-original-width 3044?><?image-scaled-height 495?><?image-scaled-width 761?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/a1db/12729497/015a605aaf93/animals-15-03603-g005.jpg?><?thumb-name animals-15-03603-g005.gif?><?thumb-size 6509?><?thumb-md5 1cb75a704d734d28b3e1460991f57e26?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 79?><?thumb-scaled-width 122?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/a1db/12729497/1cb75a704d73/animals-15-03603-g005.gif?></graphic></fig><fig position="float" id="animals-15-03603-f006" orientation="portrait"><label>Figure 6</label><caption><p>APOA1 regulates triglyceride accumulation in duck hepatocytes by modulating lipid metabolism pathways. (<bold>A</bold>) Fluorescence microscopy images confirming the successful transfection of oeAPOA1, shAPOA1, oeNC and shNC plasmids. Objective lens magnification: 20×. (<bold>B</bold>,<bold>C</bold>) The mRNA (<bold>B</bold>) and protein (<bold>C</bold>) expression levels of APOA1 were validated by qPCR and Western blot, respectively. GAPDH was used as a loading control. (<bold>D</bold>) Intracellular triglyceride (TG) content measured in the duck hepatocytes. (<bold>E</bold>) Representative images of lipid droplets stained with Oil Red O. Objective lens magnification: 20×. (<bold>F</bold>) Quantitative analysis of lipid accumulation from the Oil Red O staining shown in (<bold>E</bold>). (<bold>G</bold>) Expression levels of key lipid metabolism genes. ACACA (Acetyl-CoA carboxylase alpha), de novo lipogenesis; FASN (Fatty acid synthase), de novo lipogenesis; LPL (Lipoprotein lipase), lipoprotein triglyceride hydrolysis; CPT1 (Carnitine palmitoyltransferase 1), rate-limiting step of mitochondrial fatty acid β-oxidation; ACOX1 (Acyl-CoA oxidase 1), rate-limiting step of peroxisomal fatty acid β-oxidation; APOB (Apolipoprotein B), essential structural component of VLDL for lipid export; ACSL1 (Acyl-CoA synthetase long chain family member 1), fatty acid activation. The data are reported as the mean ± SD on the basis of n = 3 independent biological replicates (cells from distinct embryos). <sup>a,b,c</sup> Significant differences are shown in superscript letters, with different letters representing significant differences (<italic toggle="yes">p</italic> &lt; 0.05).</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" position="float" orientation="portrait" xlink:href="animals-15-03603-g006a.jpg"><?image-name animals-15-03603-g006a.jpg?><?image-size 82507?><?image-md5 cd0f3de868078a1a833d2f534c3f0d42?><?image-image-server-status LOAD_COMPLETED?><?image-original-height 1555?><?image-original-width 3136?><?image-scaled-height 389?><?image-scaled-width 784?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/a1db/12729497/cd0f3de86807/animals-15-03603-g006a.jpg?><?thumb-name animals-15-03603-g006a.gif?><?thumb-size 8431?><?thumb-md5 e790b1e59e3ea48a5414c14e82e49329?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 80?><?thumb-scaled-width 161?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/a1db/12729497/e790b1e59e3e/animals-15-03603-g006a.gif?></graphic><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" position="float" orientation="portrait" xlink:href="animals-15-03603-g006b.jpg"><?image-name animals-15-03603-g006b.jpg?><?image-size 162220?><?image-md5 aa9942035d2b36d4160642e4bad97315?><?image-image-server-status LOAD_COMPLETED?><?image-original-height 4441?><?image-original-width 3176?><?image-scaled-height 1110?><?image-scaled-width 794?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/a1db/12729497/aa9942035d2b/animals-15-03603-g006b.jpg?><?thumb-name animals-15-03603-g006b.gif?><?thumb-size 8705?><?thumb-md5 cba74b2ff56e309646b5c85d7eb6673b?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 140?><?thumb-scaled-width 100?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/a1db/12729497/cba74b2ff56e/animals-15-03603-g006b.gif?></graphic></fig></floats-group></article>